# Sentient Pi — deploy-time variables.
#
# Provider keys, voice IDs, admin secrets are all entered through the webui
# setup wizard at https://<pi-ip>:8888 on first launch. Don't put any of
# those here — they live in ~/.sentient/secrets/keys.yaml, managed by the
# wizard.
#
# `python3 deploy/setup-prod.py` writes this file for you (auto-detects
# HOST_DOCKER_GID). Manual setup:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host docker socket access (REQUIRED).
#
# The gateway calls the docker API over /var/run/docker.sock to spawn its
# sibling service containers. The host docker group's GID is passed into
# the container with `group_add` so the gateway process can write the socket.
#
# Linux/Pi:
#   HOST_DOCKER_GID=$(getent group docker | cut -d: -f3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOST_DOCKER_GID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — host timezone. Defaults to America/Vancouver inside compose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TZ=America/Vancouver

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — host path of an existing TLS cert dir to reuse instead of the
# gateway's self-signed default (e.g. a Let's-Encrypt-managed dir already
# shared with another container on the host).
#
# Set by `setup-prod.py` when the operator answers the cert-reuse prompt.
# The script symlinks ~/.sentient/certs/{cert,key}.pem → ${HOST_CERT_DIR}/
# {fullchain,key}.pem, and compose bind-mounts this path into the container
# at the same path so the symlinks resolve.
#
# Leave blank when not reusing a cert — the gateway generates self-signed
# certs at boot. Default mount target then collapses to ~/.sentient/certs
# (already bind-mounted at /app/certs).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST_CERT_DIR=/path/to/your/cert/dir
